A||N||12||wxxo||rear wing?||||1||
Z||000000||wxxo||05-30-2000||01:36 PM||||is there a difference between the rear wings on fieros?? always see rear wings for 86 gt or for a formula. are they not all the same?? if not what is the difference? tia||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-30-2000||02:25 PM||||A stock Fiero wing is a stock Fiero wing.  There wasn't any difference between the earliest ('84 Indy) to the latest ('88 Formula or GT).  I believe you could order a wing on any of the 375,000 Fieros.  Some of the models came more or less "standard" with a wing (usually all of the GTs, the Formula, and the Indy plus alot of the '86 and '87 SEs).||||reg||1
Z||000002||wxxo||05-30-2000||04:58 PM||||thanks. thats what i was thinking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||05-30-2000||06:26 PM||||There are reproduction wings that may be out there.  They may be slightly different.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||05-30-2000||08:38 PM||||The factory wing has 2 different mounting locations in them. If you take the gaskets off the stands you will see 3 holes. The front hole will be used in both notchback and fastback models, but the middle one is for the rear when used on a notchback and the one to the rear is used for fastbacks. These are only holes and the bolts can be pulled out and installed in either hole.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||05-31-2000||12:03 AM||||The fastback wing is slightly taller than the notchback wing.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||05-31-2000||12:24 AM||||I need to check where the wing from my '87 GT came from...looks totally different from the wing on my Coupe.<P>Ozzy<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierodave||05-31-2000||06:39 AM||||MOnkey Is correct!  there all the same. None are taller or different!<BR>there are some that have weathered differnt over the years, and have sags in them giving the impression there taller because the tips are higher on the ends due to a slight sag in the middle of the wing!<BR>they all Have the same part number from 84-88 (same numbers on my 86 GT 84 Indy and the 88 I sold last summer) and the stock stands are all the same hieght.<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||05-31-2000||12:12 PM||||Just for grins...<BR>A&A Fiberglass makes a reproduction wing that appears to match the original quite closely.<BR>Check this link... <A HREF="http://www.a-aspec.com/media/2712.GIF" TARGET=_blank>http://www.a-aspec.com/media/2712.GIF</A> <BR>Their home page is  <A HREF="http://www.a-aspec.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.a-aspec.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||TheFiero64||05-31-2000||03:37 PM||||I have the A&A wing on my 88 coupe. Looks like my GT's stock wing but the stands are molded in. <B>Best part is that it was $149 brand new!</B>||||reg||10
